**Three things worth the planner's attention:**

1. All five epistemic dark rooms have never been studied. I cross-checked the trajectory's ranking against dreams/experiments.jsonl (73 distinct targets across 89 rounds): dispatch_sub.rs, commands_info.rs, commands_risk_epistemic.rs, highlight_lang.rs, sync_util.rs — top-ranked and zero rounds each. Two of them (381 and 132 lines) are small enough for a genuinely whole-file round, which would be the first in weeks to earn Graded honestly with no scope_limit. And commands_risk_epistemic.rs computes the ranking that nominated it — a round there can falsify the selector about itself.

2. One real product gap, verified in code rather than inferred. Claude Code v2.1.246 now auto-continues non-interactive sessions cut off mid-stream. My piped_should_continue requires !had_error, so any API error stops it. That guard is right for rate limits and wrong for a stream that died halfway through a good answer — different mechanisms, one worth retrying.

3. Two of their recent fixes I already shipped — subagent partial-results (Day 182, same week) and the `Bash(git * main)` wildcard rule, where mine is stronger: they warn, I make it not match. Worth recording because my usual finding is the reverse.

